WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Take a position that feels supported.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.015
Keep your eyes open if you prefer.

3
00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:26.950
Notice the general shape of this moment without trying to improve it: the body here, the room around you, and whatever mood or energy has arrived.

4
00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:38.014
Find one place where effort is useful.

5
00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:44.729
Perhaps the back is holding you upright or the feet are keeping balance.

6
00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:49.029
Let that necessary effort remain.

7
00:00:57.284 --> 00:01:01.774
Now look for effort that may not be needed.

8
00:01:03.474 --> 00:01:11.680
Check the space between the eyebrows, the tongue, the fingers, and the shoulders.

9
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.110
Do not order anything to relax.

10
00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:23.570
Ask whether one area can use slightly less force.

11
00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:41.742
Feel one breath pass through the body without changing it.

12
00:01:43.442 --> 00:01:48.007
On the exhale, imagine no special release.

13
00:01:49.707 --> 00:01:55.827
Simply notice whether the body makes any adjustment by itself.

14
00:02:09.586 --> 00:02:13.141
If tension stays, let it stay.

15
00:02:14.841 --> 00:02:17.001
Soften the attention around it.

16
00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:27.226
Sense the nearby areas, the support beneath it, and the space around the body.

17
00:02:28.926 --> 00:02:33.466
One tight place does not have to become the whole field.

18
00:02:47.224 --> 00:02:48.144
Check the jaw.

19
00:02:49.844 --> 00:02:54.284
The teeth can remain separated if that is comfortable.

20
00:02:55.984 --> 00:03:00.024
Let the lips find their own position.

21
00:03:01.724 --> 00:03:03.364
Then notice the hands.

22
00:03:05.064 --> 00:03:10.474
Feel each hand's weight rather than asking it to become loose.

23
00:03:24.233 --> 00:03:34.453
Notice any effort in the mind: rehearsing, solving, or insisting that this practice work.

24
00:03:36.153 --> 00:03:42.213
See whether the next few seconds can remain unresolved.

25
00:03:43.913 --> 00:03:48.258
A thought may continue without being completed now.

26
00:04:05.456 --> 00:04:10.376
Return to the useful effort that supports your posture.

27
00:04:12.076 --> 00:04:13.316
Keep what is needed.

28
00:04:15.016 --> 00:04:23.151
Allow what is not needed to become five percent quieter, if it wants to.

29
00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.750
Feel the room again.

30
00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:46.470
Let your gaze move and make a small, comfortable adjustment.

31
00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:53.655
Softening is not collapse and it does not erase difficulty.

32
00:04:55.355 --> 00:05:00.000
It is a little more room around what is already here.
